  "notes": "SERIES BREAK: Months 2024-09 to 2025-12 are on the old CPI base 2012=100. From 2026-01 the series is the new CPI base 2024=100 (first released 12 Feb 2026 for Jan 2026). Year-on-year rates across the break are not strictly like for like. Food is the Consumer Food Price Index (CFPI) combined, year-on-year. Latest month is Aug 2026 (released 14 Sep 2026, provisional); Sep 2026 is due about 12 Oct 2026. Values use the latest revised figure where a later release gave one (for example Jun 2026 urban 3.93, Jan 2026 2.74, Jul 2025 1.61, Sep 2025 1.44 headline and -2.33 food, Aug 2025 food -0.64). Sep 2025 rural 1.07 and urban 2.04 are from the first (provisional) release and were not checked against later revisions. Jul 2026 values are provisional (a secondary source shows 4.44 for Jul, unverified). Rural and urban are null for 2025-01 to 2025-07 because those releases were not fetched. Aug 2026 group values come from secondary news reports quoting the MoSPI release; the MoSPI or PIB Aug 2026 press note itself was not fetched. In the new series there is no separate fuel and light group: it is folded into Housing, water, electricity, gas and fuels. The tolerance band of 2 to 6% around a 4% target is the standard RBI framework, repeated in the secondary sources but not read from an RBI page here."
